% 12-FLOAT: THE FLOAT STACK AND FLOAT WORDS (STOIC FLOAT).  FLOATS ARE
% D_FLOATING ON THE FLOAT STACK, R7.
FLOAT< DECIMAL
".=      " MSG 1.5 .= SPACE 0. .= SPACE -2.25 .= SPACE 1000000. .= SPACE .001 .= CR
"I->F    " MSG 7 I->F .= CR
"F->I    " MSG 3.7 F->I = -3.7 F->I = CR
"ARITH   " MSG 1.5 2.25 .+ .= SPACE 10. 4. .- .= SPACE 3. 4. .* .= SPACE 1. 4. ./ .= CR
"MINUS   " MSG 2.5 .MINUS .= CR
"POWER   " MSG 2. 10. .^ .= CR
"F=      |" MSG 3.14159 8 3 F= "|" MSG -3.14159 8 2 F= "|" MSG CR
"E=      |" MSG 12345.6 12 3 E= "|" MSG CR
"CMP     " MSG 1. 2. .GT = 2. 1. .GT = 1. 1. .EQ = 1. .GTZ = CR
"STACK   " MSG 1. 2. .SWAP .= SPACE .= SPACE 1. 2. .OVER .= SPACE .= SPACE .= CR
% .FLIP MOVES ONLY THE FIRST LONGWORD OF EACH D_FLOATING VALUE
"FLIP    " MSG 1.1 2.2 3.3 .FLIP .= SPACE .= SPACE .= CR
"ROT     " MSG 1. 2. 3. .+ROT .= SPACE .= SPACE .= SPACE 1. 2. 3. .-ROT .= SPACE .= SPACE .= CR
2.5 'FV .VARIABLE
"VAR     " MSG FV .@ .= SPACE 4.5 FV .! FV .? CR
% IN DECIMAL "E" IS NOT A DIGIT, SO 1.E30 WOULD BE UNDEFINED; IN HEX IT IS
HEX
"BIG     " MSG 1.E30 .= CR
% PAST ABOUT 1.7E38 IS A FLOATING OVERFLOW TRAP.  A RUN-TIME ERROR ENDS
% ONLY ITS LINE; A LOAD FILE GOES ON (A COMPILE ERROR ENDS THE FILE)
"OVERFLOW " MSG 1.E30 1.E30 .* .= CR
DECIMAL
% F= WITH TOO SMALL A FIELD ABORTS THE LINE
"F= ERR  " MSG 3.14159 2 3 F= "NOT REACHED" MSG CR
"NEXT LINE" MSG CR
